#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The wallet subsytem provides a convenient and secure way to manage all your "
"passwords."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#: index.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid "<keyword>KDE</keyword>"
msgstr "<keyword>KDE</keyword>"

#. Tag: keyword
#: index.docbook:45
#, no-c-format
msgid "Kwallet"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#: index.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid "passwords"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#: index.docbook:47
#, no-c-format
msgid "forms"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:53
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Computer users have a very large amount of data to manage, some of which is "
"sensitive. In particular, you will typically have many passwords to manage. "
"Remembering them is difficult, writing them down on paper or in a text file "
"is insecure, and using tools such at PGP is tedious and inconvenient."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kwallet; saves this sensitive data for you in a strongly encrypted file, "
"accessible by all applications, and protected with a master password that "
"you define."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kwallet; supports multiple wallets, so for the most secure operation, you "
"should use one wallet for local passwords, and another for network passwords "
"and form data. You can configure this behavior in the &kwallet; "
"&kcontrolcenter; module, however the default setting is to store everything "
"in one wallet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:73
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A wallet is by default closed, which means that you must supply a password "
"to open it. Once the wallet is opened, the contents can be accessed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kwalletmanager;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kwalletmanager; serves a number of functions. Firstly it allows you to see "
"if any wallets are open, which wallets those are, and which applications are "
"using each wallet. You can disconnect an application's access to a wallet "
"from within the &kwalletmanager;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may also manage the wallets installed on the system, creating and "
"deleting wallets and manipulating their contents (changing keys, ...)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Normally the &kwalletmanager; application is launched when &kde; starts and "
"remains in iconic form in the system tray. Alternatively, when a wallet is "
"opened, the &kwalletmanager; application will be launched. A system tray "
"icon indicates that a wallet is open: <mediaobject> <imageobject> <imagedata "
"fileref=\"cr22-action-wallet_open.png\"/> </imageobject> </mediaobject> When "
"all wallets are closed, the icon will reflect this by showing a closed "
"wallet:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click once on the system tray wallet icon to display the &kwalletmanager; "
"window showing all available wallets as icons which reflect their current "
"status, either open or closed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kwalletmanager; Context Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<mousebutton>Right</mousebutton> clicking on a wallet in the "
"&kwalletmanager; window offers the following functions:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid "New Wallet..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Create a new wallet. A dialog box will ask you for the name of the new "
"wallet that you want to create."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:140
#, no-c-format
msgid "<shortcut>&Enter;</shortcut> <guisubmenu>Open...</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Open the wallet. Opening the wallet causes the contents of the wallet to be "
"displayed in a new window where you can add, delete, or modify the contents "
"of the wallet. You may also double click the wallet icon to cause it to "
"open. If the wallet is not already open, you will be requested to enter the "
"password. See below for details of using the wallet window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid "Change Password"
msgstr "Modificar lo mot de pas"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:163
#, no-c-format
msgid "Change the master password for the wallet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guisubmenu
#: index.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid "Disconnect"
msgstr "Desconnectar"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Disconnect an application from the wallet. Currently connected applications "
"will appear in a submenu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:174
#, no-c-format
msgid "Close"
msgstr "Tampar"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid "Force the wallet to be closed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: index.docbook:179
#, no-c-format
msgid "Delete"
msgstr "Suprimir"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid "Delete the wallet"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Wallet Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Double clicking on a wallet in the &kwalletmanager; window will open a new "
"window displaying that wallet's contents. A wallet may contain any number of "
"folders, which allow storing of password information. By default a wallet "
"will contain folders named Form Data and Passwords."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:196
#, no-c-format
msgid "The window has four panes:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid "A summary of the contents of the current folder"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:208
#, no-c-format
msgid "The folders contained in the wallet"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid "The entries in the currently selected folder"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid "The contents of the selected folder entry"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:214
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Folders may be added or deleted, and selecting a folder will update the "
"folder entry list and the summary display. Selecting a folder entry will "
"update the entry contents pane, and allow you to edit that entry."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Entries may also be created or deleted via the context menu for the folder "
"contents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"All folders and entries may be dragged and dropped into other wallets or "
"folders respectively. This allows a user to easily package up a new wallet "
"for transfer to another environment. For instance, a new wallet could be "
"created and copied onto a removable flash memory device. Important passwords "
"could be transferred there, so you have them available in other locations."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:241
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuring &kwallet;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:244
#, no-c-format
msgid "Wallet Preferences"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:246
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kwallet; contains a small configuration panel with several options that "
"allow you to tune &kwallet; to your personal preferences. The default "
"settings for &kwallet; are sufficient for most users."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Check the box to enable or disable the &kde; wallet subsystem entirely. If "
"this box is unchecked, then &kwallet; is entirely disabled and none of the "
"other options here have any effect, nor will &kwallet; record any "
"information, or offer to fill in forms for you."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:256
#, no-c-format
msgid "Close Wallet"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:258
#, no-c-format
msgid "Close when unused for:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Close the current wallet after a period of inactivity. If you check this "
"option, set the period in the box, default is 10 minutes. When a wallet is "
"closed, the password is needed to access it again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:267
#, no-c-format
msgid "Close when screen saver starts"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:269
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Close the wallet as soon as the screen saver starts. When a wallet is "
"closed, the password is needed to access it again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:275
#, no-c-format
msgid "Close when last application stops using it"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Close the wallet as soon as applications that use it have stopped. Note that "
"your wallets will only be closed when all the applications that use it have "
"stopped. When a wallet is closed, the password is needed to access it again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:286
#, no-c-format
msgid "Automatic Wallet Selection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:288
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select wallet to use as default:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:290
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select which wallet you want to use as default wallet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:295
#, no-c-format
msgid "Different wallet for local passwords:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:297
#, no-c-format
msgid "If checked, choose a different wallet for local passwords."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:303
#, no-c-format
msgid "Wallet Manager"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:305
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show manager in system tray"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:307
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enable the wallet manager to have its icon in the system tray."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:312
#, no-c-format
msgid "Hide System tray icon when last wallet closes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:315
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When there is no wallet in use anymore, remove the wallet icon from the "
"system tray."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:321
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Finally, there is a button labelled <guibutton>Launch Wallet Manager</"
"guibutton>, which does precisely that."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:326
#, no-c-format
msgid "Access Control"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:328
#, no-c-format
msgid "There is only one option on this page:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:332
#, no-c-format
msgid "Prompt when an application accesses an open wallet"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:334
#, no-c-format
msgid "Signal you when an application gains access to an open wallet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:339
#, no-c-format
msgid "Next there is a tree style view of the access controls for your wallets."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&LMB; click on the <guiicon>+</guiicon> symbol beside a wallet name to "
"expand the tree. You will see the name of each application that has asked "
"for access to the wallet, and the policy you set for it. You cannot edit "
"policies here, or add them, but it is possible to delete an entry by &RMB; "
"clicking on it and choosing <guimenuitem>Delete</guimenuitem> From the "
"context menu that appears, or by simply selecting it and pressing the "
"<keycap>Delete</keycap> key."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:354
#, no-c-format
msgid "Advanced Features"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:356
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Wallets can be dragged from the &kwalletmanager; window. This allows you to "
"drag the wallet to a file browser window, where you can choose to copy, "
"move, or link the wallet, as desired."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:360
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You might use this to save a wallet to portable media, such as a USB "
"keychain, so that you can take your passwords with you to work or on a "
"vacation, and still have easy access to important sites."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:364
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Future versions will have built-in functions for easy export or copying of "
"data to portable devices."
msgstr ""

